    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d83">

                <pb facs="0336" n="296" xml:id="pg296"/>

                <head>83. Instruction From the Department of State to
                        All Embassies in the American Republics<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d83-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">CA–534</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1959-07-16"><hi rendition="#italic">July 16,
                        1959</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <list type="simple">
                    <head>SUBJECT</head>
                    <item>The Caribbean Situation</item>
                </list>
                <p>Enclosed for your background information are copies of three memoranda of
                    conversation concerning the Caribbean situation. The Department feels that the
                    line taken by Mr. Rubottom in these
                    conversations might serve as valuable background for ARA Chiefs of Mission in connection with any similar
                    conversations.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold"
                            >Dillon</hi></signed></closer>




                <xi:include href="d83-a1.xml" xpointer="d83-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d83-a2.xml" xpointer="d83-a2"/>
                <xi:include href="d83-a3.xml" xpointer="d83-a3"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
